[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3]

; CLUSTER LAUNCHER, in the player's hands.
;
; SAME HOLDER AS THE MARK ONE AND THE SQUAD AUTOMATIC — scale 0.26 at
; (0.104, -0.123, -0.55) — because the model is built to the same scale and
; axes. That is what lets one ADS solve serve all three.
;
; ADS SOLVE — and this is the ONE weapon whose ads_rotation is not zero.
;
; The other two keep a flat sight line so the bore stays on the crosshair. A
; launcher wants the bore ABOVE the line of sight, because the shell falls the
; whole way. So the rear reticle sits high and the pose pitches the gun nose-up
; by ads_rotation.z = 4.661 degrees, which levels the 50m mark's sight line AND
; elevates the bore by exactly that much:
;
;   range = v^2 sin(2 theta) / g = 55^2 * sin(9.322 deg) / 9.8 = 50.0 m
;
; So the crosshair means 50m, and the other three marks mean what the table in
; cluster_launcher_model.tscn says they mean.
;
; DEGREES, NOT RADIANS. This field read 0.0813502, which IS 4.661 degrees — in
; radians. The right angle in the wrong unit. Every pose in PlayerEquipment is
; degrees and update_view() writes rotation_degrees, so the game pitched the
; launcher by 0.08 of a degree and the crosshair meant about 1.7m instead of 50.
; preview_viewmodel.gd and preview_gl_ranges.gd both posed in radians as well,
; which is why the range pictures looked right while the game did not: the tools
; agreed with each other and with nothing the player ever saw. Both pose in
; degrees now, and tools/test_viewmodel_poses.gd holds the whole stack to it.
;
; ads_position is metres and needed no conversion — it was solved against the
; model pitched by this same 4.661 degrees, which is what the pose stack now
; actually applies. x puts the 50m mark 0.278m from the eye; z = -0.4 centres it.
;
; THE SHELL MUST LEAVE ALONG THE BORE, not the camera. See _fire_shot() in
; player_cluster_launcher.gd — firing down the view axis would throw it flat
; and make every mark on that leaf decorative.
;
; SIX ROUNDS, THEN FIVE AND A HALF SECONDS. That reload is the weapon's price:
; the drum is a burst of area control and then you are carrying a club.

